Day 65 – Terraform Modules

Today I learned the basics of Terraform Modules.

Topics Covered

- What are Terraform Modules?
- Root Module vs Child Module
- Custom EC2 Module
- Custom Security Group Module
- Module Variables
- Module Outputs
- Basic Dynamic Blocks
- Calling Child Modules from Root Module

Module Structure

terraform-modules/
├── main.tf
├── variables.tf
├── outputs.tf
├── providers.tf
└── modules/
    ├── ec2-instance/
    │   ├── main.tf
    │   ├── variables.tf
    │   └── outputs.tf
    └── security-group/
        ├── main.tf
        ├── variables.tf
        └── outputs.tf

Key Learning

Terraform Modules help us create reusable infrastructure code instead of repeating the same configuration.

I also learned how variables provide inputs to modules and outputs return useful information from modules.

Commands Practiced

terraform init
terraform validate
